    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "GVM Auctioneers are delighted to introduce to the market this attractive three-bedroom bungalow, ideally positioned on a superb circa 0.25-acre private site in the highly sought-after Ballyclough area, on the outskirts of Limerick City.\n\nCombining spacious accommodation, mature gardens and excellent future potential, this property offers a rare opportunity to acquire a home in one of Limerick`s most established residential locations.\n\nWhile it would benefit from some updating and modernisation, it can be comfortably occupied from day one, allowing a new owner to make improvements gradually and at their own pace. Alternatively, it presents an exciting opportunity for a purchaser wishing to undertake a more comprehensive renovation and create a home tailored to their own requirements in one of Limerick`s most desirable residential locations.\n\nThe mature and private site is a particular feature of the property. Generous established gardens provide an excellent sense of space and seclusion, while the size of the site also offers considerable potential to extend or enhance the existing accommodation, subject to the necessary planning permission.\n\nThe location is truly second to none. The lush, manicured fairways of Limerick Golf Club are just a short distance away, while the highly regarded Roxboro Primary School is also within easy reach. Raheen Business Park, Crescent Shopping Centre and University Hospital Limerick are all just a few minutes` drive away, while excellent access to the nearby Motorway places the national road network conveniently on your doorstep.\n\nProperties combining such a convenient and sought-after location with a mature private site and this level of future potential rarely come to the market. Whether seeking a comfortable home to enjoy and update gradually, or a property with scope to extend, renovate and create something truly individual, this Ballyclough bungalow presents an opportunity not to be missed.\n\nEarly viewing is strongly recommended to fully appreciate the setting, potential and all that this property has to offer.\n\nKey Features:\n\nHighly Sought-After Ballyclough Location: Superb residential setting close to Limerick Golf Club and Roxboro Primary School.\n\nExcellent Connectivity: Just minutes from Raheen Business Park, Crescent Shopping Centre and University Hospital Limerick, with convenient access to the nearby motorway network.\n\nPrivate c. 0.25-Acre Site: Mature, established gardens offering an excellent sense of privacy and space, together with potential to extend, subject to the necessary planning permission.\n\nBright & Spacious Accommodation: Three bedrooms, two reception rooms including an exceptionally spacious rear living room, kitchen, modern family bathroom, utility room and guest WC.\n\nMove-In Ready: Presented in exceptionally clean and comfortable condition, allowing a purchaser to move in immediately and modernise gradually over time.\n\nExcellent Future Potential: Equally suited to buyers wishing to undertake a more comprehensive renovation or explore the possibilities for extending and enhancing the existing accommodation\n\nThis house has been vacant for a number of years and should qualify for all the excellent vacant home grants (subject to terms & conditions)\n\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance hall - 4.04m (13'3\") x 1.04m (3'5\")\nBright and inviting\n\nSitting room - 4.02m (13'2\") x 3.03m (9'11\")\nWith fireplace and overlooking the front garden\n\nkitchen - 4.02m (13'2\") x 3.05m (10'0\")\nWith tiled flooring, built in floor and eye level presses and solid fuel stove\n\nUtility - 3.02m (9'11\") x 2.04m (6'8\")\nPlumbed with wc & whb off\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.01m (9'11\") x 3.02m (9'11\")\nDouble. built in wardrobes\n\nBedroom 2 - 4.02m (13'2\") x 3.02m (9'11\")\nDouble with built in wardrobes\n\nBedroom 3 - 4m (13'1\") x 3.01m (9'11\")\nDouble with built in wardrobes\n\nBathroom - 2.06m (6'9\") x 1.06m (3'6\")\nNewly fitted and tiled\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Garage attached </li><li> Oil fired central heating system </li><li> Septic tank & mains water </li><li> Ready for occupation and no chain </li><li> Good on site parking and circulation </li><li> Double glazed UPVC woodgrain windows </li><li> Very welcoming local community with excellent sporting and educational facilities </li><li> Attractive price point</li></ul>"
      },
